          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Career and Awards</strong><br>\nWeinberg held positions at several prestigious institutions, including MIT, Harvard, and the University of Texas at Austin. He received numerous awards throughout his career, in addition to the Nobel Prize, such as the National Medal of Science.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Views and Philosophy</strong><br>\nWeinberg was also known for his personal views and philosophical perspectives, especially regarding religion and secularism. He famously said, \"With or without religion, you would have good people doing good things and evil people doing evil things. But for good people to do evil things, that takes religion.\"</p>\n\n<p><strong>His Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nSteven Weinberg passed away on July 23, 2021, leaving behind a vast legacy in the field of physics. His work continues to influence the way we understand the fundamental forces and particles of the universe. He is remembered as one of the most influential physicists of the 20th century.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
